# LEVEL 5 - A SAFE IMAGE: NOT ROOT, AND A HEALTHCHECK
#
# Start from your Dockerfile.4. Then add:
#
# TODO 1: do NOT run the app as "root". If somebody breaks into the app, "root" in the container
#         is very powerful. Create a normal user and switch to it:
#             RUN useradd --create-home app
#             USER app
#         (Put the USER line AFTER the lines that need root, and make sure the user can read /app.)
#
# TODO 2: a HEALTHCHECK. Docker runs a command every few seconds. If it fails, the container
#         is marked "unhealthy". The image has curl:
#             HEALTHCHECK --interval=5s --timeout=3s --retries=3 CMD curl -f http://localhost:8080/health || exit 1
#
# The checker runs the container, asks /whoami (it must NOT say root), and waits until Docker
# says the container is "healthy".
